/-!
# The tensor von Neumann algebras `M ⊗ 1` and `1 ⊗ M`

Using the operator amplifications `amplifyLeft : B(H₁) → B(H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)`, `A ↦ A ⊗̂ 1`, and
`amplifyRight : B(H₂) → B(H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)`, `B ↦ 1 ⊗̂ B` (from `TensorProductCompletion`), a von Neumann
algebra `M` on `H` gives two von Neumann algebras on a completed Hilbert tensor product:

* `M ⊗ 𝟙[K] = VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne M K` on `H ⊗̂ K` — the von Neumann algebra generated by
  `M ⊗ 1 = {A ⊗̂ 1 | A ∈ M}`,
* `𝟙[K] ⊗ M = VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor K M` on `K ⊗̂ H` — the von Neumann algebra generated by
  `1 ⊗ M = {1 ⊗̂ B | B ∈ M}`.

For `M = B(H)` they are the two tensor factors `𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂] = B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` and
`𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂) = 1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)` of `B(H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)`.

Here and in the files downstream, `⊗̄` is documentation shorthand for the von Neumann (spatial)
tensor product of algebras: it has no Lean declaration, and the algebras it names are the ones
above. The tensor notations that *are* declared are `⊗̂` for the completed Hilbert
tensor product, `⊗ₕ` for elementary tensors, `𝟙 ⊗ B` and `A ⊗ 𝟙` for the amplified operators
(all in `TensorProductCompletion`), and `M ⊗ 𝟙[K]`, `𝟙[K] ⊗ M` for the algebras of this file.

These are the objects in the split-property tensor decomposition `A₁ ⊆ B(H₁)⊗̄1`,
`A₂ ⊆ 1⊗̄B(H₂)` — equation (39) of J. Yngvason, *Localization and Entanglement in Relativistic
Quantum Physics*, in *The Message of Quantum Science*, Lecture Notes in Physics 899, Springer 2015,
pp. 325–348 (arXiv:1401.2652), §5.1. The file culminates in the **tensor commutation theorem**
`(𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂])′ = 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂)` (von Neumann's commutation theorem for a full factor on
the first leg): the commutant of `B(H₁)⊗̄1` is exactly `1⊗̄B(H₂)`.

The algebra `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` is `1 ⊗ M` itself (`VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_oneTensor_iff`), via the slice
lemma `HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes`. The commutants `(M ⊗ 1)′ = M′ ⊗̄ B(H₂)` and
`(1 ⊗ M)′ = B(H₁) ⊗̄ M′` of a general `M` are not formalised.

## Main definitions

* `VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne M K` — the von Neumann algebra generated by `M ⊗ 1`.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor K M` — the von Neumann algebra generated by `1 ⊗ M`.
* `HilbertTensor.tmulRightL f` — the inclusion `H₂ → H₁ ⊗̂ H₂`, `z ↦ f ⊗ z`.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensorEquiv H₁ M` — the `⋆`-isomorphism `x ↦ 1 ⊗ x` of `M` onto
  `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` (for nontrivial `H₁`).
* `HilbertTensor.amplifyLeftStarAlgEquiv` — the `⋆`-isomorphism `A ↦ A ⊗ 1` of `B(H₁)` onto
  `𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]` (for nontrivial `H₂`).

## Main results

* `VonNeumannAlgebra.amplifyLeft_mem_tensorOne` / `VonNeumannAlgebra.amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor` —
  `x ⊗ 1 ∈ M ⊗ 𝟙[K]` and `1 ⊗ x ∈ 𝟙[K] ⊗ M` for `x ∈ M`.
* `HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight` — the two amplifications commute.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_of_commutes` — the slice lemma: an
  operator commuting with all `A ⊗̂ 1` lies in `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂)`.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant` /
  `VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_commutant` — the tensor commutation theorem
  `(B(H₁)⊗̄1)′ = 1⊗̄B(H₂)` and its bicommutant companion.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.isFactor_tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators` /
  `VonNeumannAlgebra.isFactor_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators` — both tensor factors are factors:
  an operator in `M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]` and in `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ N` is a scalar
  (`VonNeumannAlgebra.eq_smul_one_of_mem_tensorOne_of_mem_oneTensor`).
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.amplifyRight_mem_commutant_oneTensor` — `1 ⊗ x′ ∈ (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M)′` for `x′ ∈ M′`.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_oneTensor_iff`, `VonNeumannAlgebra.coe_oneTensor` — `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M = 1 ⊗ M`.
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.inner_apply_eq_of_mem_generated` — two vector functionals that agree on a
  unital `⋆`-subalgebra `A` agree on the von Neumann algebra it generates (by the density form of
  the bicommutant theorem).
* `VonNeumannAlgebra.inner_apply_eq_of_mem_oneTensor` — hence vector functionals on `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M`
  are determined by their values on `1 ⊗ M`.

## Notation

`M ⊗ 𝟙[K]` is `VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne M K`, the algebra `M ⊗ 1` on `H ⊗̂ K`, and `𝟙[K] ⊗ M` is
`VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor K M`, the algebra `1 ⊗ M` on `K ⊗̂ H`; activate them with
`open scoped VonNeumannAlgebra`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct InnerProduct VonNeumannAlgebra HilbertTensor

namespace VonNeumannAlgebra

open HilbertTensor (amplifyLeft amplifyRight)

variable {H₁ H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]

/-- The von Neumann algebra `M ⊗ 1` on `H ⊗̂ K` of a von Neumann algebra `M` on `H`: the von
Neumann algebra generated by the left amplifications `x ⊗̂ 1`, `x ∈ M`. For `M = 𝓑(H)` it is the
tensor factor `B(H) ⊗̄ 1`. -/
noncomputable def tensorOne (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) (K : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup K]
    [InnerProductSpace ℂ K] : VonNeumannAlgebra (H ⊗̂ K) :=
  generated (amplifyLeft (H₂ := K) '' (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))

/-- `M ⊗ 𝟙[K]` is `VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne M K`, the von Neumann algebra `M ⊗ 1` on
`H ⊗̂ K`. -/
scoped notation:100 M:101 " ⊗ " "𝟙[" K "]" => VonNeumannAlgebra.tensorOne M K

variable (H₁) in
/-- The von Neumann algebra `1 ⊗ M` on `H₁ ⊗̂ H` of a von Neumann algebra `M` on `H`: the von
Neumann algebra generated by the right amplifications `1 ⊗̂ x`, `x ∈ M`. For `M = 𝓑(H)` it is the
tensor factor `1 ⊗̄ B(H)`. -/
noncomputable def oneTensor (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : VonNeumannAlgebra (H₁ ⊗̂ H) :=
  generated (amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) '' (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)))

/-- `𝟙[K] ⊗ M` is `VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor K M`, the von Neumann algebra `1 ⊗ M` on
`K ⊗̂ H`. -/
scoped notation:100 "𝟙[" K "]" " ⊗ " M:101 => VonNeumannAlgebra.oneTensor K M

variable {M N : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H}

/-- `x ⊗ 1 ∈ M ⊗ 𝟙[H₁]` for `x ∈ M`. -/
lemma amplifyLeft_mem_tensorOne (hx : x ∈ M) : amplifyLeft (H₂ := H₁) x ∈ M ⊗ 𝟙[H₁] :=
  mem_generated_of_mem ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- `1 ⊗ x ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` for `x ∈ M`. -/
lemma amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor (hx : x ∈ M) : amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) x ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M :=
  mem_generated_of_mem ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- `M ⊗ 𝟙[H₁]` is monotone in `M`. -/
lemma tensorOne_mono (h : M ≤ N) : M ⊗ 𝟙[H₁] ≤ N ⊗ 𝟙[H₁] :=
  generated_mono (Set.image_mono h)

/-- `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` is monotone in `M`. -/
lemma oneTensor_mono (h : M ≤ N) : 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M ≤ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ N :=
  generated_mono (Set.image_mono h)

end VonNeumannAlgebra

namespace HilbertTensor

variable {H₁ H₂ : Type*}
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₂]

/-! ### The slice lemma

An operator `T` commuting with every `A ⊗̂ 1` must be of the form `1 ⊗̂ S`, where
`S = ι_e* ∘ T ∘ ι_e` for a fixed unit vector `e ∈ H₁` and `ι_e : H₂ → H₁ ⊗̂ H₂`, `y ↦ e ⊗ y`. The
reduction to a pure-tensor computation uses the rank-one operators `|f⟩⟨e|` on `H₁`. -/

/-- The bounded inclusion `H₂ → H₁ ⊗̂ H₂`, `z ↦ f ⊗ z`, for a fixed `f ∈ H₁`. Its operator norm
is `‖f‖` (`‖tmulRightL f z‖ = ‖f‖ * ‖z‖`), so it is an isometry exactly when `‖f‖ = 1`. -/
noncomputable def tmulRightL (f : H₁) : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ :=
  UniformSpace.Completion.toComplL.comp
    (LinearMap.mkContinuous (TensorProduct.mk ℂ H₁ H₂ f) ‖f‖ fun z => by
      rw [TensorProduct.mk_apply, TensorProduct.norm_tmul])

/-- The inclusion `tmulRightL f` sends `z` to the elementary tensor `f ⊗ z`. -/
@[simp] lemma tmulRightL_apply (f : H₁) (z : H₂) : tmulRightL f z = tmul f z := rfl

/-- The left and right amplifications commute: `(A ⊗̂ 1)(1 ⊗̂ B) = A ⊗̂ B = (1 ⊗̂ B)(A ⊗̂ 1)`, also
for `A : H₁ → H₃` between different first factors. -/
lemma amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight {H₃ : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H₃] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₃]
    (A : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₃) (B : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂) :
    (amplifyLeft (H₂ := H₂) A).comp (amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) B)
      = (𝟙 ⊗ B).comp (A ⊗ 𝟙) := by
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
  refine UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on w
    (isClosed_eq (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop)) (fun a => ?_)
  induction a using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul f y =>
      change (A ⊗ 𝟙) ((𝟙 ⊗ B) (tmul f y)) = (𝟙 ⊗ B) ((A ⊗ 𝟙) (tmul f y))
      rw [amplifyRight_tmul, amplifyLeft_tmul, amplifyLeft_tmul, amplifyRight_tmul]
  | add p q hp hq => rw [UniformSpace.Completion.coe_add, map_add, map_add, hp, hq]

/-- For `H₁ = 0` the operator algebra on `H₁ ⊗̂ H₂` is trivial: `1 = 1 ⊗̂ 1 = 0 ⊗̂ 1 = 0`. -/
private lemma subsingleton_of_subsingleton_left [Subsingleton H₁] :
    Subsingleton (H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂) :=
  subsingleton_of_zero_eq_one <| by
    rw [← amplifyLeft_zero (H₂ := H₂), ← amplifyLeft_one, Subsingleton.elim (0 : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁) 1]

section CompleteRight

variable [CompleteSpace H₂]

/-- The adjoint of the inclusion `ι_e` acts on pure tensors as the `e`-slice
`g ⊗ z ↦ ⟪e, g⟫ • z`. -/
lemma adjoint_tmulRightL_tmul (e g : H₁) (z : H₂) :
    ((tmulRightL (H₂ := H₂) e)†) (tmul g z) = (inner ℂ e g) • z := by
  refine ext_inner_right ℂ fun y => ?_
  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left, tmulRightL_apply, inner_tmul, inner_smul_left,
    inner_conj_symm]

/-- The amplification of a rank-one operator `|f⟩⟨e|` factors through the `e`-slice and the
inclusion `ι_f`: `(|f⟩⟨e|) ⊗̂ 1 = ι_f ∘ ι_e*`. This is the algebraic heart of the slice
argument. -/
lemma amplifyLeft_rankOne_eq (e f : H₁) :
    amplifyLeft (H₂ := H₂) (InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e)
      = (tmulRightL f).comp ((tmulRightL e)†) := by
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
  refine UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on w
    (isClosed_eq (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop)) (fun a => ?_)
  induction a using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul g z =>
      change (_ ⊗ 𝟙) (tmul g z)
        = (tmulRightL f).comp ((tmulRightL e)†) (tmul g z)
      rw [amplifyLeft_tmul, ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, adjoint_tmulRightL_tmul,
        tmulRightL_apply, InnerProductSpace.rankOne_apply,
        tmul_smul_left, smul_tmul_right]
  | add p q hp hq => rw [UniformSpace.Completion.coe_add, map_add, map_add, hp, hq]

/-- **Slice lemma (dense form, explicit representation).** If `T` commutes with the rank-one
amplifications `(|f⟩⟨e|) ⊗̂ 1` for `f` ranging over a set `D` whose span is dense in `H₁` (and a
fixed unit vector `e ∈ H₁`), then `T = 1 ⊗̂ S` for `S = ι_e* ∘ T ∘ ι_e`. The relation
`T (f ⊗̂ y) = f ⊗̂ (S y)` is first established for `f ∈ D` and then extended to all `f` by density,
working at the level of the bounded inclusions `ι_y : f ↦ f ⊗̂ y`. -/
lemma exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes_dense (e : H₁) (he : ‖e‖ = 1) (D : Set H₁)
    (hD : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ D : Set H₁))
    (T : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)
    (hT : ∀ f ∈ D, T.comp ((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙)
      = ((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙).comp T) :
    ∃ S : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂, T = 𝟙 ⊗ S := by
  set S := ((tmulRightL e)†).comp (T.comp (tmulRightL e)) with hS
  have hee : inner ℂ e e = (1 : ℂ) := by rw [inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, he]; norm_num
  have key : ∀ f ∈ D, ∀ y : H₂, T (tmul f y) = tmul f (S y) := by
    intro f hf y
    have e1 : amplifyLeft (H₂ := H₂) (InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) (tmul e y) = tmul f y := by
      rw [amplifyLeft_tmul, InnerProductSpace.rankOne_apply, hee, one_smul]
    calc T (tmul f y)
        = T (((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙) (tmul e y)) := by rw [e1]
      _ = ((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙) (T (tmul e y)) := by
            rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, hT f hf, ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply]
      _ = (tmulRightL f).comp ((tmulRightL e)†) (T (tmul e y)) := by
            rw [amplifyLeft_rankOne_eq]
      _ = tmul f (S y) := by
            rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, tmulRightL_apply, hS]
            simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, tmulRightL_apply]
  have key_all : ∀ (f : H₁) (y : H₂), T (tmul f y) = tmul f (S y) := by
    intro f y
    have hcl : T.comp (tmulLeftL y) = (𝟙 ⊗ S).comp (tmulLeftL y) := by
      refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext_on hD (fun g hg => ?_)
      rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, tmulLeftL_apply,
        amplifyRight_tmul, key g hg y]
    have h := congrArg (fun L : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ => L f) hcl
    simpa only [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, tmulLeftL_apply, amplifyRight_tmul] using h
  have hTS : T = 𝟙 ⊗ S := by
    refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
    refine UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on w
      (isClosed_eq T.continuous (𝟙 ⊗ S).continuous) (fun a => ?_)
    induction a using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | tmul f y =>
        change T (tmul f y) = (𝟙 ⊗ S) (tmul f y)
        rw [key_all, amplifyRight_tmul]
    | add p q hp hq => rw [UniformSpace.Completion.coe_add, map_add, map_add, hp, hq]
  exact ⟨S, hTS⟩

/-- **Slice lemma (explicit representation).** If `T` commutes with every left amplification
`A ⊗̂ 1`, then `T = 1 ⊗̂ S`: for `H₁ = 0` every operator is `0 = 1 ⊗̂ 0`, and otherwise
`S = ι_e* ∘ T ∘ ι_e` for a unit vector `e ∈ H₁`. -/
lemma exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes (T : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)
    (hT : ∀ A : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁, T.comp (A ⊗ 𝟙) = (A ⊗ 𝟙).comp T) :
    ∃ S : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂, T = 𝟙 ⊗ S := by
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial H₁ with _ | _
  · have := subsingleton_of_subsingleton_left (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H₂)
    exact ⟨0, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_ne (0 : H₁)
  have he : ‖(‖u‖⁻¹ : ℂ) • u‖ = 1 := by
    rw [norm_smul, norm_inv, Complex.norm_real, norm_norm,
      inv_mul_cancel₀ (norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr hu)]
  exact exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes_dense _ he Set.univ
    (by rw [Submodule.span_univ, Submodule.top_coe]; exact dense_univ) T
    (fun f _ => hT (InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f _))

end CompleteRight

/-- For `H₁ = 0` all von Neumann algebras on `H₁ ⊗̂ H₂` coincide: each contains `1`, which is
every operator. -/
lemma vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_of_subsingleton_left [Subsingleton H₁]
    (M N : VonNeumannAlgebra (H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)) : M = N := by
  have := subsingleton_of_subsingleton_left (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H₂)
  ext x
  rw [Subsingleton.elim x 1]
  exact iff_of_true M.one_mem N.one_mem

/-- The right amplification `B ↦ 1 ⊗̂ B` is injective (for nontrivial `H₁`): evaluating on pure
tensors `f ⊗̂ y` with `f ≠ 0` recovers `B y` up to the norm factor `‖f‖`. -/
lemma amplifyRight_injective [Nontrivial H₁] :
    Function.Injective (amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H₂)) := by
  intro B₁ B₂ h
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_ne (0 : H₁)
  ext y
  have h1 := congrArg
    (fun L : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ => L (tmul f y)) h
  simp only [amplifyRight_tmul] at h1
  have h2 : tmul f (B₁ y - B₂ y) = 0 := by
    rw [sub_eq_add_neg, tmul_add, ← neg_one_smul ℂ (B₂ y), smul_tmul_right, h1, neg_one_smul,
      add_neg_cancel]
  have h3 : ‖f‖ * ‖B₁ y - B₂ y‖ = 0 := by rw [← norm_tmul, h2, norm_zero]
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h3 with h4 | h4
  · exact absurd (norm_eq_zero.mp h4) hf
  · exact sub_eq_zero.mp (norm_eq_zero.mp h4)

/-- The left amplification `A ↦ A ⊗̂ 1` is injective (for nontrivial `H₂`): evaluating on pure
tensors `x ⊗̂ g` with `g ≠ 0` recovers `A x` up to the norm factor `‖g‖`. -/
lemma amplifyLeft_injective [Nontrivial H₂] :
    Function.Injective (amplifyLeft (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H₂) (H₃ := H₁)) := by
  intro A₁ A₂ h
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_ne (0 : H₂)
  ext x
  have h1 := congrArg
    (fun L : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ => L (tmul x g)) h
  simp only [amplifyLeft_tmul] at h1
  have h2 : tmul (A₁ x - A₂ x) g = 0 := by
    rw [sub_eq_add_neg, add_tmul, ← neg_one_smul ℂ (A₂ x), tmul_smul_left, h1, neg_one_smul,
      add_neg_cancel]
  have h3 : ‖A₁ x - A₂ x‖ * ‖g‖ = 0 := by rw [← norm_tmul, h2, norm_zero]
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h3 with h4 | h4
  · exact sub_eq_zero.mp (norm_eq_zero.mp h4)
  · exact absurd (norm_eq_zero.mp h4) hg

end HilbertTensor

/-! ### The tensor commutation theorem

The commutant of `B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` is exactly `1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)` — von Neumann's commutation theorem for the
special case of a full factor on the first leg. The hard inclusion `(B(H₁)⊗̄1)′ ⊆ 1⊗̄B(H₂)` is the
slice lemma `HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes`. -/

namespace VonNeumannAlgebra

open HilbertTensor (amplifyLeft amplifyRight)

variable {H₁ H₂ : Type*}
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₂]

/-- Every right amplification `1 ⊗̂ B` commutes with `M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]`, i.e. lies in its commutant. -/
lemma amplifyRight_mem_commutant_tensorOne [CompleteSpace H₁] {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H₁}
    (B : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂) : amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) B ∈ (M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂])′ := by
  rw [tensorOne, commutant_generated, mem_commutantSet_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨A, -, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight A B
  · rw [HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_star, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight (star A) B

section CompleteRight

variable [CompleteSpace H₂]

/-- **Slice lemma (dense form).** If `T` commutes with the rank-one amplifications
`(|f⟩⟨e|) ⊗̂ 1` for `f` ranging over a set `D` whose span is dense in `H₁` (and a fixed unit
vector `e ∈ H₁`), then `T = 1 ⊗̂ S`, hence `T ∈ 1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)`. -/
lemma mem_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_of_commutes_dense (e : H₁) (he : ‖e‖ = 1) (D : Set H₁)
    (hD : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ D : Set H₁))
    (T : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)
    (hT : ∀ f ∈ D, T.comp ((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙)
      = ((InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ f e) ⊗ 𝟙).comp T) :
    T ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂) := by
  obtain ⟨S, rfl⟩ := HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes_dense e he D hD T hT
  exact amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor (mem_boundedLinearOperators S)

/-- **Slice lemma (hard inclusion of the commutation theorem).** If `T` commutes with every left
amplification `A ⊗̂ 1`, then `T = 1 ⊗̂ S` (`HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes`),
hence `T ∈ 1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)`. -/
lemma mem_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_of_commutes (T : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂)
    (hT : ∀ A : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁, T.comp (A ⊗ 𝟙) = (A ⊗ 𝟙).comp T) :
    T ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂) := by
  obtain ⟨S, rfl⟩ := HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes T hT
  exact amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor (mem_boundedLinearOperators S)

end CompleteRight

/-- **Tensor commutation theorem.** The commutant of the von Neumann factor `B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` is exactly
`1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)`. This is von Neumann's commutation theorem `(M ⊗ 1)' = M' ⊗ B(H₂)` for `M = B(H₁)`
(whose commutant `M'` is `ℂ`), and it is the analytic core of the split-property tensor
decomposition: combined with a unit vector in `H₁`, it identifies `A₁ ⊆ B(H₁)⊗̄1` with
`A₂ ⊆ 1⊗̄B(H₂)` for commuting `A₁, A₂`. -/
theorem tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant [CompleteSpace H₁] [CompleteSpace H₂] :
    (𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂])′ = 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · -- hard inclusion: every `T` commuting with `B(H₁)⊗̄1` lies in `1⊗̄B(H₂)`
    intro T hT
    refine mem_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_of_commutes T fun A => ?_
    rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact (mem_commutant_iff.mp hT _
      (amplifyLeft_mem_tensorOne (mem_boundedLinearOperators A))).symm
  · -- easy inclusion: `1⊗̄B(H₂)` commutes with `B(H₁)⊗̄1`
    refine generated_le ?_
    rintro _ ⟨B, -, rfl⟩
    exact amplifyRight_mem_commutant_tensorOne B

/-- The commutant of `1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)` is exactly `B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1`: the bicommutant form of the tensor
commutation theorem `tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant`. -/
theorem oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_commutant [CompleteSpace H₁] [CompleteSpace H₂] :
    (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂))′ = 𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂] := by
  rw [← tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant, commutant_commutant]

/-! ### The tensor factors are factors -/

/-- **The centre of the tensor decomposition is trivial.** An operator lying in both
`M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂] ⊆ B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` and `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ N ⊆ 1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)` is a scalar: by the slice lemma it is
`1 ⊗̂ S`, membership in `B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1 = (1 ⊗̄ B(H₂))'` makes `S` commute with all of `B(H₂)` — in
particular with every rank-one operator — so `S` is scalar. -/
lemma eq_smul_one_of_mem_tensorOne_of_mem_oneTensor [CompleteSpace H₁] [CompleteSpace H₂]
    {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H₁} {N : VonNeumannAlgebra H₂} {x : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂}
    (hL : x ∈ M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]) (hR : x ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ N) : ∃ c : ℂ, x = c • 1 := by
  replace hL : x ∈ 𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂] :=
    tensorOne_mono (fun y _ => mem_boundedLinearOperators y) hL
  replace hR : x ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂) :=
    oneTensor_mono (fun y _ => mem_boundedLinearOperators y) hR
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial H₁ with _ | _
  · have := HilbertTensor.subsingleton_of_subsingleton_left (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H₂)
    exact ⟨0, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  rw [← tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant] at hR
  obtain ⟨S, rfl⟩ := HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes x fun A => by
    rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact (mem_commutant_iff.mp hR _
      (amplifyLeft_mem_tensorOne (mem_boundedLinearOperators A))).symm
  have hS : ∀ B : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂, S * B = B * S := by
    intro B
    have hmem : amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) S ∈ (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂))′ := by
      rw [oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_commutant]; exact hL
    have h1 := mem_commutant_iff.mp hmem (𝟙 ⊗ B)
      (amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor (mem_boundedLinearOperators B))
    apply HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_injective (H₁ := H₁)
    rw [HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul, HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul]
    exact h1.symm
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ :=
    ContinuousLinearMap.exists_eq_smul_one_of_forall_rankOne_comm (S := S) fun a b => by
    rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact hS (InnerProductSpace.rankOne ℂ a b)
  exact ⟨c, by rw [hc, HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_smul, HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_one]⟩

/-- **`B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` is a factor**: its centre is trivial, since by the commutation theorem the
centre is `(B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1) ⊓ (1 ⊗̄ B(H₂))`. -/
theorem isFactor_tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators [CompleteSpace H₁] [CompleteSpace H₂] :
    IsFactor (𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]) := fun _ hx hx' =>
  eq_smul_one_of_mem_tensorOne_of_mem_oneTensor hx
    (by rwa [← tensorOne_boundedLinearOperators_commutant])

/-- **`1 ⊗̄ B(H₂)` is a factor**: its centre is trivial, since by the commutation theorem the
centre is `(B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1) ⊓ (1 ⊗̄ B(H₂))`. -/
theorem isFactor_oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators [CompleteSpace H₁] [CompleteSpace H₂] :
    IsFactor (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ 𝓑(H₂)) := fun _ hx hx' =>
  eq_smul_one_of_mem_tensorOne_of_mem_oneTensor
    (by rwa [← oneTensor_boundedLinearOperators_commutant]) hx

/-- **Every element of `M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]` is a left amplification `A ⊗̂ 1`.** An element `T` of
`M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]` commutes with every right amplification (`amplifyRight_mem_commutant_tensorOne`);
transporting through the swap equivalence `HilbertTensor.commEquiv` turns this into commutation
with every left amplification on the swapped space, where the slice lemma
`HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes` produces the operator. -/
lemma exists_amplifyLeft_of_mem_tensorOne [CompleteSpace H₁]
    {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H₁} {T : H₁ ⊗̂ H₂ →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H₂} (hT : T ∈ M ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]) :
    ∃ A : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁, T = A ⊗ 𝟙 := by
  have hcomm : ∀ B : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂, T * 𝟙 ⊗ B = 𝟙 ⊗ B * T := fun B =>
    mem_commutant_iff.mp (amplifyRight_mem_commutant_tensorOne B) T hT
  have hhyp : ∀ A : H₂ →L[ℂ] H₂,
      (HilbertTensor.commEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv T).comp (A ⊗ 𝟙)
        = (A ⊗ 𝟙).comp (HilbertTensor.commEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv T) := fun A => by
    rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def,
      ← HilbertTensor.conjStarAlgEquiv_commEquiv_amplifyRight A, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, hcomm A]
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes (H₁ := H₂) (H₂ := H₁)
    (HilbertTensor.commEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv T) hhyp
  refine ⟨S, ?_⟩
  have hsymm := congrArg (⇑HilbertTensor.commEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv.symm) hS
  rw [StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, HilbertTensor.conjStarAlgEquiv_symm_commEquiv_amplifyRight]
    at hsymm
  exact hsymm

end VonNeumannAlgebra

/-! ### `B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` is `⋆`-isomorphic to `B(H₁)`

The left amplification `(: ⊗ 𝟙) B(H₁) → B(H₁)⊗̄1` is a `⋆`-algebra homomorphism that is
injective (`amplifyLeft_injective`) and surjective onto `𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]`
(`VonNeumannAlgebra.exists_amplifyLeft_of_mem_tensorOne`). Hence it is a `⋆`-isomorphism
`B(H₁) ≃⋆ₐ B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` (`amplifyLeftStarAlgEquiv`). -/

namespace HilbertTensor

variable {H₁ H₂ : Type*}
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₁] [CompleteSpace H₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup H₂] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₂]

/-- The left amplification as a unital `⋆`-algebra homomorphism `B(H₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` onto the
factor, i.e. with codomain restricted to `𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]`. -/
noncomputable def amplifyLeftVnₐ : (H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]) where
  toFun A := ⟨A ⊗ 𝟙, VonNeumannAlgebra.amplifyLeft_mem_tensorOne
    (VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_boundedLinearOperators A)⟩
  map_one' := Subtype.ext amplifyLeft_one
  map_mul' A B := Subtype.ext (amplifyLeft_mul A B)
  map_zero' := Subtype.ext amplifyLeft_zero
  map_add' A B := Subtype.ext (amplifyLeft_add A B)
  commutes' r := Subtype.ext <| by
    simp [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, amplifyLeft_smul, amplifyLeft_one]
  map_star' A := Subtype.ext (amplifyLeft_star A).symm

/-- **`B(H₁) ⊗̄ 1` is `⋆`-isomorphic to `B(H₁)`.** The left amplification is a `⋆`-isomorphism of
`B(H₁)` onto the factor `𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]`, for nontrivial `H₂`. -/
noncomputable def amplifyLeftStarAlgEquiv [Nontrivial H₂] :
    (H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] (𝓑(H₁) ⊗ 𝟙[H₂]) :=
  StarAlgEquiv.ofBijective amplifyLeftVnₐ
    ⟨fun A B hAB => amplifyLeft_injective (H₂ := H₂) (Subtype.ext_iff.mp hAB),
     fun ⟨T, hT⟩ => by
       obtain ⟨A, rfl⟩ := VonNeumannAlgebra.exists_amplifyLeft_of_mem_tensorOne hT
       exact ⟨A, rfl⟩⟩

end HilbertTensor

/-! ### The von Neumann algebra `1 ⊗ M` -/

open scoped InnerProductSpace VonNeumannAlgebra HilbertTensor
open HilbertTensor (amplifyLeft amplifyRight amplifyRightₐ)

namespace VonNeumannAlgebra

section Generated

variable {K : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup K] [InnerProductSpace ℂ K] [CompleteSpace K]

/-- **Vector functionals on a generated von Neumann algebra.** If the vector functionals of `Ξ`
and `Ξ′` agree on a unital `⋆`-subalgebra `A`, they agree on the von Neumann algebra `A″`
generated by `A`: `A″` is the weak-operator closure of `A`, and `y ↦ ⟪Ξ, y Ξ⟫` is
weak-operator continuous. -/
lemma inner_apply_eq_of_mem_generated (A : StarSubalgebra ℂ (K →L[ℂ] K)) {Ξ Ξ' : K}
    (h : ∀ x ∈ A, ⟪Ξ, x Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', x Ξ'⟫_ℂ) {y : K →L[ℂ] K}
    (hy : y ∈ generated (A : Set (K →L[ℂ] K))) : ⟪Ξ, y Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', y Ξ'⟫_ℂ := by
  have hstar : star (A : Set (K →L[ℂ] K)) = A :=
    Set.ext fun x => ⟨fun hx => by simpa using star_mem (s := A) hx,
      fun hx => Set.mem_star.mpr (star_mem (s := A) hx)⟩
  have hy' : y ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (A : Set (K →L[ℂ] K))) := by
    rw [← coe_generated_of_star_eq hstar]
    exact hy
  have hmem : ContinuousLinearMapWOT.ofCLM y ∈
      closure (WeakOperatorTopology.Set.toWOT (H := K) (A.toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra : Set (K →L[ℂ] K))) := by
    rw [NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.wotClosure_eq_doubleCommutant A.toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra
      (InnerProductSpace.actsNondegenerately_of_one_mem A.one_mem)]
    exact hy'
  have hclosed : IsClosed {T : K →WOT[ℂ] K | ⟪Ξ, T Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', T Ξ'⟫_ℂ} :=
    isClosed_eq (ContinuousLinearMapWOT.continuous_dual_apply Ξ (innerSL ℂ Ξ))
      (ContinuousLinearMapWOT.continuous_dual_apply Ξ' (innerSL ℂ Ξ'))
  exact closure_minimal (t := {T : K →WOT[ℂ] K | ⟪Ξ, T Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', T Ξ'⟫_ℂ}) (fun T hT => h _ hT)
    hclosed hmem

end Generated

variable {H₁ H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H₁] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]

variable {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H} {x : H →L[ℂ] H}

/-- `1 ⊗ x′` commutes with `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` for `x′ ∈ M′`. -/
lemma amplifyRight_mem_commutant_oneTensor (hx : x ∈ M′) :
    amplifyRight (H₁ := H₁) x ∈ (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M)′ := by
  rw [oneTensor, commutant_generated, mem_commutantSet_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  have hy' : star y ∈ M := star_mem hy
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul, ← HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul,
      mem_commutant_iff.mp hx y hy]
  · rw [HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_star, ← HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul,
      ← HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul, mem_commutant_iff.mp hx _ hy']

/-- **Vector functionals on `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M`** are determined by their values on `1 ⊗ M`. -/
lemma inner_apply_eq_of_mem_oneTensor {Ξ Ξ' : H₁ ⊗̂ H}
    (h : ∀ x ∈ M, ⟪Ξ, (𝟙 ⊗ x) Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', (𝟙 ⊗ x) Ξ'⟫_ℂ) {y : H₁ ⊗̂ H →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H}
    (hy : y ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M) : ⟪Ξ, y Ξ⟫_ℂ = ⟪Ξ', y Ξ'⟫_ℂ := by
  refine inner_apply_eq_of_mem_generated (M.toStarSubalgebra.map (𝟙 ⊗ₐ)) ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact h x hx
  · rwa [StarSubalgebra.coe_map]

/-- `A ⊗ 1` commutes with `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` for every `A ∈ B(H₁)`. -/
lemma amplifyLeft_mem_commutant_oneTensor (A : H₁ →L[ℂ] H₁) :
    amplifyLeft (H₂ := H) A ∈ (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M)′ := by
  rw [oneTensor, commutant_generated, mem_commutantSet_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨x, -, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact (HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight A x).symm
  · rw [HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_star, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact (HilbertTensor.amplifyLeft_comp_amplifyRight A (star x)).symm

/-- **`𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` is `1 ⊗ M`.** The elements of `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` are exactly the `1 ⊗ x` with
`x ∈ M` (for `H₁ = 0` both sides are `{0}`). -/
theorem mem_oneTensor_iff {y : H₁ ⊗̂ H →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H} :
    y ∈ 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M ↔ ∃ x ∈ M, 𝟙 ⊗ x = y := by
  refine ⟨fun hy => ?_, fun ⟨x, hx, h⟩ => h ▸ amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor hx⟩
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial H₁ with _ | _
  · have := HilbertTensor.subsingleton_of_subsingleton_left (H₁ := H₁) (H₂ := H)
    exact ⟨0, M.zero_mem, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := HilbertTensor.exists_amplifyRight_of_commutes y fun A => by
    rw [← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def, ← ContinuousLinearMap.mul_def]
    exact mem_commutant_iff.mp (amplifyLeft_mem_commutant_oneTensor A) y hy
  refine ⟨x, ?_, rfl⟩
  rw [← commutant_commutant M, mem_commutant_iff]
  intro z hz
  apply HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_injective (H₁ := H₁)
  rw [HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul, HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_mul]
  exact (mem_commutant_iff.mp (amplifyRight_mem_commutant_oneTensor (H₁ := H₁) hz) _ hy).symm

/-- **`𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M` is `1 ⊗ M`**, as sets. -/
lemma coe_oneTensor :
    (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M : Set (H₁ ⊗̂ H →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H)) = (𝟙 ⊗ ·) '' (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) :=
  Set.ext fun _ => mem_oneTensor_iff

variable (H₁ M) in
/-- For a nontrivial `H₁`, `x ↦ 1 ⊗ x` is a `⋆`-isomorphism of `M` onto `𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M`
(`VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_oneTensor_iff`). -/
noncomputable def oneTensorEquiv [Nontrivial H₁] : M ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M :=
  StarAlgEquiv.ofBijective
    (((𝟙 ⊗ₐ).comp M.toStarSubalgebra.subtype).codRestrict (𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M).toStarSubalgebra
      fun x => amplifyRight_mem_oneTensor x.2)
    ⟨fun _ _ h => Subtype.ext (HilbertTensor.amplifyRight_injective (congrArg Subtype.val h)),
      fun y => by
        obtain ⟨x, hx, h⟩ := mem_oneTensor_iff.mp y.2
        exact ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, Subtype.ext h⟩⟩

/-- `oneTensorEquiv H₁ M x = 1 ⊗ x`. -/
@[simp]
lemma coe_oneTensorEquiv_apply [Nontrivial H₁] (x : M) :
    ((oneTensorEquiv H₁ M x : 𝟙[H₁] ⊗ M) : H₁ ⊗̂ H →L[ℂ] H₁ ⊗̂ H) = 𝟙 ⊗ (x : H →L[ℂ] H) :=
  rfl

/-- `oneTensorEquiv H₁ M 1 = 1`. -/
lemma oneTensorEquiv_one [Nontrivial H₁] : oneTensorEquiv H₁ M 1 = 1 :=
  map_one _

end VonNeumannAlgebra
